<http://openvivo.org/a/doi10.1007/s13596-016-0255-5> a ns5:BFO_0000001,
        ns5:BFO_0000002,
        ns5:BFO_0000031,
        ns5:IAO_0000030,
        ns3:AcademicArticle,
        ns3:Article,
        ns3:Document,
        ns11:Thing ;
    rdfs:label "Immunomodulatory properties and biomarkers characterization of novel Withania somnifera based formulation supplemented with minerals in Sprague Dawley rats" ;
    ns5:ARG_2000028 <http://openvivo.org/a/n129099> ;
    ns3:abstract "<p>Herbomineral formulations have been accepted world-wide due to its significant therapeutic outcomes. The study aimed to evaluate the immunomodulatory potential of novel herbomineral formulation (TEBEH) on Sprague Dawley rats using cyclophosphamide-induced immunosuppression. Major immune related parameters were monitored such haemagglutination assay, delayed type hypersensitivity reaction, cellular immune response (CD4+ and CD8+), IgG and IgM, hematological analysis, antioxidant profile, and estimation of major lipid biomarkers. The study results suggest herbomineral formulation significantly (p &le; 0.05) improved the concentration of primary and secondary titre by 41.18 and 68%. However, the rat paw edema at 24 h showed increased edema by 77.78% (p &le; 0.01). Herbomineral formulation exhibited increase in the CD4+ and CD8+ counts in animals by 28.03 and 60.70%, respectively. In addition, the concentrations of IgM and IgG were improved by 14.29 and 8.26% respectively. Besides, other supportive parameter such as hematology and antioxidant profile was significantly (p &le; 0.001) improved, while free radical, lipid peroxidation was decreased. Moreover, the major lipid biomarkers were improved such as decreased triglycerides, LDL and VLDL by 15.88, 3.65, and 16.01%, respectively. Overall, the promising results of this study indicated that the herbomineral formulation, TEBEH can be employed to improve the cellular and humoral immunity along with improved hematological, antioxidant, and lipid profile.</p>" ;
    ns3:doi "10.1007/s13596-016-0255-5" ;
    ns3:issue "1" ;
    ns3:numPages "10"^^xsd:long ;
