    rdfs:label "Aaron Braun"@en-US ;
    ns5:ARG_2000028 <http://openvivo.org/a/n52552> ;
    ns2:modTime "2018-02-28T13:38:42"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    ns2:mostSpecificType ns8:Person ;
    ns7:mainImage <http://openvivo.org/a/n46509> ;
    ns9:networkId "0000-0002-7310-6661" ;
    ns1:orcidId <http://orcid.org/0000-0002-7310-6661> ;
    ns1:overview """<p>Aaron Braun grew up in Fort Collins Colorado. He is a professional runner and <a href="http://scholar.google.com/citations?user=lWU2xwYAAAAJ&amp;hl=en" title="Google scholar">researcher in the fields of sport</a>, healthcare, and&nbsp;nutrition. He has done many&nbsp;types of research&nbsp;about the relationship between energy levels and food.</p>\r
<p>Aaron started his running career in the 7th grade. In high&nbsp;school,&nbsp;Aaron only had PR&rsquo;s of 9:34 3200 and 4:24 1600. He holds a Bachelor degree in Mathematics and a Masters degree in Exercise Science from the Adams State University. He became successful while running for the division 2 powerhouse Adams State, the university he attended. He captured 16 All American honors and 6 National titles. He ran times of 13:36 (5k), 3:39 (altitude adjusted 1500), and 4:01 (mile) at Adams.</p>\r
<p>Aaron began training with the NAZ Elite team in the fall of 2016. He officially signed on in March of 2017. He is&nbsp;one&nbsp;of the most flexible professional distance runners in&nbsp;the US&nbsp;which are competing today. With PRs of 13:20.25 for 5,000m, 27:41.52 for 10,000m, 1:01:38 for the Half Marathon and 2:12:54 in the Marathon, he can compete at the highest level at just about every distance. PRO STATS 2012 - finished 5th at the US Olympic Trials over 10,000m. 2013 - won the US 12k National Championships and two months later ran a breakthrough&nbsp;half-marathon&nbsp;personal best of 1:01:38. In 2015 he ran 2:12:54 to finish as the top American at the Chevron Houston Marathon.</p>\r
<p>In 2016 - returned to racing with a win at the Big Sur Half Marathon. 2017 - won the Credit Union Sactown 10 miler in April in his first race as an official member of the team. Aaron Braun has a big comeback in the fall of 2017 when he ran 2:13:41 at the Chicago Marathon where he was 12th overall and the 3rd American.</p>\r
<p>Catch up with Aaron Braun on <a href="https://runnerstips101.wordpress.com/" title="runners tips">his blog</a> where he writes about common issues related to athletics and running.</p>""" ;
